h2 { "Iteration, generics and explicit traits" }

Option[T], the uninhabited primitive never, reusable Iterable sources and owned Iterator[T, E] cursors provide typed iteration and error channels. std/iter.map, filter and take compose lazy pipelines. Breaking out of iteration closes its cursor. Generator cleanup settles owned resources and cancels/joins unfinished children; children may keep running while the generator is paused. Eligible local scalar pipelines are fused conservatively, while escaping or effectful cursors retain their frames.

Static generics support generic functions/types, explicit trait/impl conformance, associated types/errors, qualified calls and generic trait parameters. Conformance is deliberate rather than inferred from matching method names. Dispatch is static, without a user class hierarchy or runtime trait objects.

Standard contracts include Equal; Order, Ordering, compare and totalCompare; stable sortedBy/sortBy; Display; and Add[Rhs], Sub[Rhs], Mul[Rhs], Div[Rhs], Rem[Rhs] and Neg with associated Output. Custom operators use ordinary evaluation, ownership and error rules. Arithmetic conformance does not grant mutation permission or automatically make a method GPU-compatible.

