h2 { "Applications and host utilities" }

table {
  row = ["Module or feature", "What is available"],
  row = ["Application entry", "main() or main(args: [String]) returns unit or ExitStatus {code: u8}. Arguments exclude the executable name. Console output is explicit."],
  row = ["std/io", "Console/error output and bounded line input with typed IoError values."],
  row = ["std/fmt", "Literal-template formatting, explicit Display implementations, checked precision/alignment/hexadecimal controls and Unicode-scalar widths."],
  row = ["std/fs", "Owned files, incremental byte/text/line I/O, buffering, seeking, directory iterators, metadata, directory creation and file/empty-directory removal."],
  row = ["std/buffer", "Owned growable ByteBuffer, capacity management, array conversion and direct filesystem buffer I/O."],
  row = ["std/parse", "Checked parsing for all ten numeric primitives and bool, with typed failures and tested floating-point rounding."],
  row = ["std/path and std/env", "Path operations and environment lookup."],
  row = ["std/time", "Monotonic Instant/Duration values and cancellable sleep that releases the task's worker."]
}

File handles and directory cursors close deterministically. finish flushes and consumes a buffered writer. Filesystem readInto, readAppend, write and writeAll accept buffers alongside their supported array forms. These are host services, including in mixed CPU/Metal/Vulkan/CUDA applications. std/process supplies application exit status; OS subprocess spawning is not part of this release.

