h2 { "GPU language coverage" }

Metal, Linux Vulkan and Linux CUDA support the admitted local control flow, safe mutation and device-array construction, checked transfer of supported CPU closures/captures, and device-compatible typed error handling. Eligibility follows specialized method bodies, supported values/effects and resource limits. Unsupported operations are diagnosed rather than silently executed on the CPU.

Host generators and I/O coexist with GPU work; suspended host cursor frames and host services are not device instructions. GPU strings/text and user-written low-level kernels remain separate work. Existing arithmetic and matmul policies retain their documented numerical contracts, including explicit software fallback where required.

Windows x86-64/ARM64 GPU packages remain experimental. Build, source compilation, relocation and package checks pass, but physical Windows GPU execution/performance remains unqualified. ARM64 compiler availability does not establish NVIDIA ARM64 driver support.

